From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:16:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] debian: Build the v4l2request hwdecs and default to them

Enable the v4l2request hwdec/interop added by the preceding patches
(https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/pull/14690). It needs an FFmpeg with the
V4L2 Request API hwdevice (AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_V4L2REQUEST); use "enabled" so
the build fails rather than silently dropping it.

This build is for boards whose video decoders are V4L2 stateless devices
(RK3588 here), which have no VA-API driver, so the shipped
/etc/mpv/mpv.conf uses hwdec=v4l2request instead of Ubuntu's hwdec=vaapi.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 debian/mpv.conf.ubuntu | 9 ++++++++-
 debian/rules           | 1 +
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian/mpv.conf.ubuntu b/debian/mpv.conf.ubuntu
index 621600c..88c8962 100644
--- a/debian/mpv.conf.ubuntu
+++ b/debian/mpv.conf.ubuntu
@@ -1 +1,8 @@
-hwdec=vaapi
+# System-wide mpv defaults (Orange Pi 5 / RK3588 build).
+# Decode with the V4L2 stateless decoders through FFmpeg's v4l2request hwaccel
+# and import the DRM PRIME (dmabuf) frames into the GPU without CPU copies.
+# Codecs or sizes the hardware can't decode fall back to software decoding.
+hwdec=v4l2request
+# EGL dmabuf import (Mesa panfrost/panthor) is the long-proven path for DRM
+# PRIME frames on Mali; to try Vulkan (panvk) instead: --gpu-api=vulkan.
+gpu-api=opengl
diff --git a/debian/rules b/debian/rules
index b52e7ea..6923f04 100755
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ override_dh_auto_configure:
 		-Dbuild-date=false \
 		-Dcdda=enabled \
 		-Ddvdnav=enabled \
+		-Dv4l2request=enabled \
 		$(ARCH_CONFIGURE)
 
 execute_after_dh_auto_install:
